    "html": "<p>This question is duplicated in #83</p>\n<p>Particle X moves in a circle with a constant speed v. The net force on X is F<sub>X</sub>. Particle Y moves with a constant velocity, the magnitude of the velocity is v. The net force on Y is F<sub>Y</sub> . Which of the following is correct?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">F<sub>X</sub><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"&gt;\"></span>F<sub>Y</sub></li><li data-label=\"B\">F<sub>X</sub><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=\"></span>F<sub>Y</sub> ≠ 0</li><li data-label=\"C\">F<sub>X </sub>&lt; F<sub>Y</sub></li><li data-label=\"D\">F<sub>X</sub><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=\"></span>F<sub>Y</sub><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=\"></span>0</li></ol>"
